ins is 30. F12: a_val 3, b_val 1 and c_val 21 (all printed) give 3 − 1 = 2 and 21 − 19 = 2, so distractor 19 is true, and a_val 3, b_val 1 and c_val 22 make distractor 20 true. The packet shows no joint constraint on a, b and c that would rule these out, so the domains as declared let a learner see a true statement keyed False. F14 wraps F11 and F12 and is the learner-facing question, so it is listed as failing too. Scope concern, not the basis of the FAIL: F14 asks learners to judge a claim as True or False, and the competency names writing an equivalent expression; the judgment form does not ask learners to write. The hint families F01 to F06 and the question families F07 to F10 print only in-vocabulary words (total, expression, missing number, sum-like terms) and do not show a defect in the packet.\"}",
